{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,380p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aa62e3f4.py\"","aggregated_output":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom arc_utils import components_mask, get_bg, neighbors4\nimport random\n\n\ndef _unique_color_with_count(counts: Counter[int], colors: list[int], target_count: int) -> int:\n    matches = [color for color in colors if counts[color] == target_count]\n    assert len(matches) == 1, \"expected a unique structural color by area\"\n    return int(matches[0])\n\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replace the outlined object with the outside contour of that outline in the marker color.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - A dominant background surrounds one 8-connected foreground outline.\n    - The outline is the unique largest foreground color.\n    - One or more smaller interior colors are inside the outline; the marker color\n      is the unique smallest non-outline color.\n\n    Rule:\n    - Erase all original foreground pixels to background.\n    - Paint every background pixel that is 4-adjacent to the outline with the\n      marker color.\n    - Keep the grid shape unchanged.\n\n    Key insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\n    largest outline supplies only the contour whose outside edge is traced.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\n\n    counts = Counter(map(int, g.flatten()))\n    foreground_colors = [color for color in counts if color != bg]\n    assert len(foreground_colors) >= 2, \"expected an outline color and a marker color\"\n\n    frame_count = max(counts[color] for color in foreground_colors)\n    frame_color = _unique_color_with_count(counts, foreground_colors, frame_count)\n    assert len(components_mask(g == frame_color, connectivity=8)) == 1, \"outline must be 8-connected\"\n\n    marker_candidates = [color for color in foreground_colors if color != frame_color]\n    marker_count = min(counts[color] for color in marker_candidates)\n    marker_color = _unique_color_with_count(counts, marker_candidates, marker_count)\n\n    out = np.full_like(g, bg)\n    contour: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n    for r, c in np.argwhere(g == frame_color):\n        for nr, nc in neighbors4(int(r), int(c)):\n            if 0 <= nr < g.shape[0] and 0 <= nc < g.shape[1] and g[nr, nc] == bg:\n                contour.add((int(nr), int(nc)))\n    assert contour, \"expected outline to touch background contour cells\"\n\n    for r, c in contour:\n        out[r, c] = marker_color\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (att2) ---------------\n\nGRID_MIN, GRID_MAX = 5, 16\nN_COLORS = 10\n\nSHAPE_MIN_HEIGHT, SHAPE_MAX_HEIGHT = 5, 7\nSHAPE_MIN_WIDTH, SHAPE_MAX_WIDTH = 3, 5\nSTART_WIDTH_MIN, START_WIDTH_MAX = 1, 2\nMAX_LOCAL_WIDTH = 5\n\nMARKER_MIN_CELLS, MARKER_MAX_CELLS = 1, 3\n\nGEN_ATTEMPTS = 300\n\nEDGE_TOUCH_TOP_BOTTOM = \"TB\"\nCORNER_EDGE_PAIRS = [\"TL\", \"TR\", \"BL\", \"BR\"]\nZERO_DELTA_SHIFTS = [-1, 0, 0, 0, 1]\n\n\ndef _gen_grow_parts(total, n):\n    n_twos = total - n\n    parts = [2] * n_twos + [1] * (n - n_twos)\n    random.shuffle(parts)\n    return parts\n\ndef _gen_drop_parts(total, n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    n_twos = random.randint(max(0, total - n), min(total // 2, n))\n    n_ones = total - 2 * n_twos\n    parts = [2] * n_twos + [1] * n_ones + [0] * (n - n_twos - n_ones)\n    random.shuffle(parts)\n    return parts\n\ndef _gen_widths(height, max_width):\n    start = random.randint(START_WIDTH_MIN, START_WIDTH_MAX)\n    diff = max_width - start\n    grow_steps = random.randint((diff + 1) // 2, min(diff, height - 1))\n    widths = [start]\n    for inc in _gen_grow_parts(diff, grow_steps):\n        widths.append(widths[-1] + inc)\n\n    remaining = height - len(widths)\n    min_end = max(1, max_width - 2 * remaining)\n    end_width = random.randint(min_end, max_width)\n    for dec in _gen_drop_parts(max_width - end_width, remaining):\n        widths.append(widths[-1] - dec)\n    return widths\n\ndef _gen_intervals(widths):\n    left, right = 0, widths[0] - 1\n    intervals = [(left, right)]\n    for prev_width, width in zip(widths, widths[1:]):\n        delta = width - prev_width\n        if delta == 2:\n            left -= 1\n            right += 1\n        elif delta == 1:\n            if random.choice([False, True]):\n                left -= 1\n            else:\n                right += 1\n        elif delta == 0:\n            shift = random.choice(ZERO_DELTA_SHIFTS) if width >= 2 else 0\n            left += shift\n            right += shift\n        elif delta == -1:\n            if random.choice([False, True]):\n                left += 1\n            else:\n                right -= 1\n        elif delta == -2:\n            left += 1\n            right -= 1\n        intervals.append((left, right))\n\n    min_left = min(l for l, _ in intervals)\n    intervals = [(l - min_left, r - min_left) for l, r in intervals]\n    if max(r for _, r in intervals) + 1 > MAX_LOCAL_WIDTH:\n        return None\n    return intervals\n\ndef _gen_local_mask(intervals):\n    height = len(intervals)\n    width = max(r for _, r in intervals) + 1\n    mask = np.zeros((height, width), dtype=bool)\n    for r, (c0, c1) in enumerate(intervals):\n        mask[r, c0 : c1 + 1] = True\n    return mask\n\ndef _gen_place_shape(grid_shape, local_mask, edge_pair):\n    rows, cols = grid_shape\n    height, width = local_mask.shape\n    if edge_pair == EDGE_TOUCH_TOP_BOTTOM:\n        if height != rows or width > cols - 2:\n            return None\n        return 0, random.randint(1, cols - width - 1)\n    if height >= rows or width >= cols:\n        return None\n    if edge_pair == \"TL\":\n        return 0, 0\n    if edge_pair == \"TR\":\n        return 0, cols - width\n    if edge_pair == \"BL\":\n        return rows - height, 0\n    return rows - height, cols - width\n\ndef _gen_full_mask(rows, cols, local_mask, r0, c0):\n    mask = np.zeros((rows, cols), dtype=bool)\n    height, width = local_mask.shape\n    mask[r0 : r0 + height, c0 : c0 + width] = local_mask\n    return mask\n\ndef _gen_layers(mask):\n    remaining = mask.copy()\n    layers = []\n    rows, cols = mask.shape\n    while np.any(remaining):\n        layer = np.zeros_like(mask)\n        for r, c in np.argwhere(remaining):\n            for nr, nc in neighbors4(int(r), int(c)):\n                if nr < 0 or nr >= rows or nc < 0 or nc >= cols or not remaining[nr, nc]:\n                    layer[r, c] = True\n                    break\n        layers.append(layer)\n        remaining[layer] = False\n    return layers\n\ndef _gen_contour(outline, shape):\n    rows, cols = shape.shape\n    contour = np.zeros_like(shape)\n    for r, c in np.argwhere(outline):\n        for nr, nc in neighbors4(int(r), int(c)):\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and not shape[nr, nc]:\n                contour[nr, nc] = True\n    return contour\n\ndef _choose_canvas_and_shape_profile():\n    rows = random.randint(GRID_MIN, GRID_MAX)\n    cols = random.randint(GRID_MIN, GRID_MAX)\n    bg = random.randrange(N_COLORS)\n\n    edge_options = []\n    if rows <= SHAPE_MAX_HEIGHT:\n        edge_options.append(EDGE_TOUCH_TOP_BOTTOM)\n    if rows >= SHAPE_MIN_HEIGHT + 1:\n        edge_options.extend(CORNER_EDGE_PAIRS)\n    if not edge_options:\n        return None\n\n    edge_pair = random.choice(edge_options)\n    height = rows if edge_pair == EDGE_TOUCH_TOP_BOTTOM else random.randint(\n        SHAPE_MIN_HEIGHT, min(SHAPE_MAX_HEIGHT, rows - 1)\n    )\n    max_width_limit = cols - 2 if edge_pair == EDGE_TOUCH_TOP_BOTTOM else cols - 1\n    if max_width_limit < SHAPE_MIN_WIDTH:\n        return None\n    max_width = random.randint(SHAPE_MIN_WIDTH, min(SHAPE_MAX_WIDTH, max_width_limit))\n\n    intervals = _gen_intervals(_gen_widths(height, max_width))\n    if intervals is None:\n        return None\n    return rows, cols, bg, edge_pair, intervals\n\ndef _build_shape(rows, cols, edge_pair, intervals):\n    local_mask = _gen_local_mask(intervals)\n    placement = _gen_place_shape((rows, cols), local_mask, edge_pair)\n    if placement is None:\n        return None\n\n    shape = _gen_full_mask(rows, cols, local_mask, *placement)\n    shape_area = int(np.sum(shape))\n    if rows * cols - shape_area <= shape_area:\n        return None\n    return shape\n\ndef _split_valid_layers(shape):\n    layers = _gen_layers(shape)\n    if len(layers) < 2:\n        return None\n\n    outline = layers[0]\n    marker = layers[-1]\n    fill = shape & ~outline & ~marker\n\n    outline_count = int(np.sum(outline))\n    marker_count = int(np.sum(marker))\n    fill_count = int(np.sum(fill))\n    if marker_count < MARKER_MIN_CELLS or marker_count > MARKER_MAX_CELLS:\n        return None\n    if len(components_mask(outline, connectivity=8)) != 1:\n        return None\n    if fill_count and not (marker_count < fill_count < outline_count):\n        return None\n    return outline, fill, marker, fill_count\n\ndef _render_input(rows, cols, bg, masks, colors):\n    outline, fill, marker = masks\n    outline_color, fill_color, marker_color = colors\n    inp = np.full((rows, cols), bg, dtype=int)\n    inp[outline] = outline_color\n    if fill_color is not None:\n        inp[fill] = fill_color\n    inp[marker] = marker_color\n    return inp\n\ndef _gen_attempt():\n    profile = _choose_canvas_and_shape_profile()\n    if profile is None:\n        return None\n    rows, cols, bg, edge_pair, intervals = profile\n\n    shape = _build_shape(rows, cols, edge_pair, intervals)\n    if shape is None:\n        return None\n\n    layer_parts = _split_valid_layers(shape)\n    if layer_parts is None:\n        return None\n    outline, fill, marker, fill_count = layer_parts\n\n    contour = _gen_contour(outline, shape)\n    if not np.any(contour):\n        return None\n\n    colors = [c for c in range(N_COLORS) if c != bg]\n    random.shuffle(colors)\n    outline_color, marker_color = colors[:2]\n    fill_color = colors[2] if fill_count else None\n    inp = _render_input(rows, cols, bg, (outline, fill, marker), (outline_color, fill_color, marker_color))\n\n    expected = np.full((rows, cols), bg, dtype=int)\n    expected[contour] = marker_color\n    if not np.array_equal(main(inp), expected):\n        return None\n    return inp\n\ndef generate_input():\n    for _ in range(GEN_ATTEMPTS):\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\n        if grid is not None:\n            return grid\n    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid aa62e3f4 input\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,640p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\"","aggregated_output":"from __future__ import annotations\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport numpy as np\nfrom arc_utils import find_components, get_bg, neighbors4, paste\nimport random\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - bg = most common color.\n    - Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n    - Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\n    Rule:\n    - Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n    - Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n    - Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\n    Key insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\n\n    def is_border(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n        return int(r) in (0, int(H - 1)) or int(c) in (0, int(W - 1))\n\n    # --- STEP 1) Detect anchors: isolated border pixels (non-bg) ---\n    anchors_by_color: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if not is_border(r, c):\n                continue\n            v = int(g[r, c])\n            if v == int(bg):\n                continue\n            ok = True\n            for rr, cc in neighbors4(int(r), int(c)):\n                if 0 <= rr < H and 0 <= cc < W and int(g[rr, cc]) != int(bg):\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            if ok and v not in anchors_by_color:\n                anchors_by_color[int(v)] = (int(r), int(c))\n\n    assert not (not anchors_by_color)\n\n    anchor_cells = {(int(r), int(c)) for (r, c) in anchors_by_color.values()}\n\n    # --- STEP 2) Extract all foreground connected components as candidate sprites. ---\n    comps = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=8, monochromatic=False, return_format=\"dict\")\n\n    def component_marker_color(coords: np.ndarray) -> int | None:\n        # For multi-color sprites, the marker color is the least frequent color inside the component.\n        vals = [int(g[int(r), int(c)]) for r, c in coords]\n        cnt = Counter(vals)\n        if len(cnt) <= 1:\n            return None\n        return int(min(cnt.items(), key=lambda kv: (int(kv[1]), int(kv[0])))[0])\n\n    def marker_pixel(coords: np.ndarray, marker: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n        # If marker appears multiple times, prefer one attached to the main body (4-adjacent to non-marker).\n        pts = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in coords if int(g[int(r), int(c)]) == int(marker)]\n        if not pts:\n            return None\n        if len(pts) == 1:\n            return pts[0]\n        S = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in coords}\n        for r, c in pts:\n            for rr, cc in neighbors4(int(r), int(c)):\n                if (int(rr), int(cc)) in S and int(g[int(rr), int(cc)]) != int(marker):\n                    return (int(r), int(c))\n        return pts[0]\n\n    moves: list[tuple[np.ndarray, int, int]] = []\n\n    for comp in comps:\n        coords = comp[\"coords\"]\n        if coords.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # --- STEP 3) Decide marker color for this component. ---\n        marker_col = component_marker_color(coords)\n        if marker_col is None:\n            # Single-color component: move only if it's a singleton of an anchor color, not the anchor itself.\n            if int(coords.shape[0]) != 1:\n                continue\n            r, c = map(int, coords[0])\n            v = int(g[r, c])\n            if v == int(bg) or v not in anchors_by_color or (r, c) in anchor_cells:\n                continue\n            marker_col = int(v)\n\n        if int(marker_col) not in anchors_by_color:\n            continue\n\n        mp = marker_pixel(coords, int(marker_col))\n        if mp is None:\n            continue\n\n        ar, ac = anchors_by_color[int(marker_col)]\n\n        # --- STEP 4) Compute translation (dr,dc). ---\n        on_top_bottom = int(ar) in (0, int(H - 1))\n        on_left_right = int(ac) in (0, int(W - 1))\n        horizontal = bool(on_top_bottom and not on_left_right)  # top/bottom but not a corner\n\n        dr = 0\n        dc = 0\n        if horizontal:\n            dc = int(ac - mp[1])\n        else:\n            dr = int(ar - mp[0])\n\n        moves.append((coords, int(dr), int(dc)))\n\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    # --- STEP 5) Apply all moves. ---\n    # Clear moved components first (prevents collisions with their original locations).\n    for coords, _dr, _dc in moves:\n        out[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] = int(bg)\n\n    # Paste moved components:\n    # - clip out-of-bounds pixels\n    # - do not overwrite existing non-bg pixels\n    for coords, dr, dc in moves:\n        for r, c in coords:\n            rr = int(r) + int(dr)\n            cc = int(c) + int(dc)\n            if 0 <= rr < H and 0 <= cc < W and int(out[rr, cc]) == int(bg):\n                out[rr, cc] = int(g[int(r), int(c)])\n\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\n\n# CFG: palette and canvas bounds.\n_COLORS = tuple(range(10))\n_BG_COLOR_RANGE = (1, 8)\n_GRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (10, 22)\n_GRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (8, 22)\n\n# CFG: placement isolation and anchor location.\n_NEIGHBORS4 = ((1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1))\n_INNER_BORDER_GAP = 1\n_ANCHOR_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\n_ISOLATION_RADIUS = 1\n\n# CFG: anchor, sprite, and retry counts.\n_ANCHOR_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 3)\n_SPRITE_COUNT_RANGE = (3, 5)\n_BODY_AREA_RANGE = (4, 13)\n_GEN_RETRY_LIMIT = 300\n\n# CFG: body geometry and shape mix.\n_BODY_HEIGHT_RANGE = (2, 5)\n_BODY_WIDTH_RANGE = (3, 7)\n_FRAME_HEIGHT_RANGE = (3, 5)\n_FRAME_WIDTH_RANGE = (3, 7)\n_FRAME_MIN_AREA = 8\n_FRAME_MAX_GAP = 3\n_FRAME_BODY_THRESHOLD = 0.28\n_WIDE_BODY_THRESHOLD = 0.55\n_SYMMETRIC_BODY_THRESHOLD = 0.82\n_SYMMETRIC_TRANSPOSE_MIN_HEIGHT = 3\n_SYMMETRIC_TRANSPOSE_PROB = 0.45\n_MARKER_INTERIOR_PROB = 0.65\n_FLIP_PROB = 0.5\n\n# CFG: optional singleton distractors.\n_DISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.15\n_DISTRACTOR_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 4)\n\n_GROW_BODY_SEEDS = [\n    {(0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0)},\n    {(0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 2)},\n    {(0, 0), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2)},\n    {(0, 2), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2)},\n    {(0, 1), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2)},\n]\n\n\ndef _norm(cells):\n    r0 = min(r for r, _c in cells)\n    c0 = min(c for _r, c in cells)\n    return {(r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in cells}\n\n\ndef _bbox(cells):\n    return (\n        min(r for r, _c in cells),\n        min(c for _r, c in cells),\n        max(r for r, _c in cells),\n        max(c for _r, c in cells),\n    )\n\n\ndef _flip(cells):\n    cells = set(cells)\n    if random.random() < _FLIP_PROB:\n        mc = max(c for _r, c in cells)\n        cells = {(r, mc - c) for r, c in cells}\n    if random.random() < _FLIP_PROB:\n        mr = max(r for r, _c in cells)\n        cells = {(mr - r, c) for r, c in cells}\n    return _norm(cells)\n\n\ndef _inclusive_range(bounds):\n    return range(int(bounds[0]), int(bounds[1]) + 1)\n\n\ndef _frontier_cells(cells, height, width):\n    \"\"\"Return empty 4-neighbor cells inside the shape canvas.\"\"\"\n    frontier = []\n    for r, c in cells:\n        for dr, dc in _NEIGHBORS4:\n            rr, cc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= rr < height and 0 <= cc < width and (rr, cc) not in cells:\n                frontier.append((rr, cc))\n    return frontier\n\n\ndef _grow_body(area):\n    choices = [\n        (h, w)\n        for h in _inclusive_range(_BODY_HEIGHT_RANGE)\n        for w in _inclusive_range(_BODY_WIDTH_RANGE)\n        if h * w >= area\n    ]\n    h, w = random.choice(choices)\n    cells = set(random.choice(_GROW_BODY_SEEDS))\n    while len(cells) < area:\n        frontier = _frontier_cells(cells, h, w)\n        if not frontier:\n            return _grow_body(area)\n        cells.add(random.choice(frontier))\n    return _flip(cells)\n\n\ndef _symmetric_body(area):\n    choices = []\n    for height in _inclusive_range(_BODY_HEIGHT_RANGE):\n        extra = area - height\n        if extra >= 2 and extra % 2 == 0 and extra // 2 <= height:\n            choices.append((height, extra // 2))\n    if not choices:\n        return _grow_body(area)\n\n    height, pair_count = random.choice(choices)\n    cells = {(r, 1) for r in range(height)}\n    rows = list(range(height))\n    random.shuffle(rows)\n    for r in rows[:pair_count]:\n        cells.add((r, 0))\n        cells.add((r, 2))\n\n    if height >= _SYMMETRIC_TRANSPOSE_MIN_HEIGHT and random.random() < _SYMMETRIC_TRANSPOSE_PROB:\n        cells = {(c, r) for r, c in cells}\n    return _flip(cells)\n\n\ndef _wide_body(area):\n    width = random.randint(_BODY_WIDTH_RANGE[0], min(_BODY_WIDTH_RANGE[1], area - 1))\n    height = random.choice([h for h in _inclusive_range(_BODY_HEIGHT_RANGE) if h * width >= area])\n    cells = {(0, c) for c in range(width)}\n    cells.add((1, random.randrange(width)))\n    while len(cells) < area:\n        frontier = _frontier_cells(cells, height, width)\n        cells.add(random.choice(frontier))\n    return _flip(cells)\n\n\ndef _frame_body(area):\n    choices = []\n    for h in _inclusive_range(_FRAME_HEIGHT_RANGE):\n        for w in _inclusive_range(_FRAME_WIDTH_RANGE):\n            perim = 2 * h + 2 * w - 4\n            removable = 2 * max(0, h - 2) + 2 * max(0, w - 2)\n            if perim >= area and perim - area <= min(_FRAME_MAX_GAP, removable):\n                choices.append((h, w))\n    if not choices:\n        return _grow_body(area)\n\n    h, w = random.choice(choices)\n    cells = {\n        (r, c)\n        for r in range(h)\n        for c in range(w)\n        if r in (0, h - 1) or c in (0, w - 1)\n    }\n    gap = len(cells) - area\n    if gap:\n        removable = [\n            (r, c)\n            for r, c in cells\n            if not (r in (0, h - 1) and c in (0, w - 1))\n        ]\n        for cell in random.sample(removable, gap):\n            cells.remove(cell)\n    return _flip(cells)\n\n\ndef _make_body(area):\n    x = random.random()\n    if area >= _FRAME_MIN_AREA and x < _FRAME_BODY_THRESHOLD:\n        return _frame_body(area)\n    if x < _WIDE_BODY_THRESHOLD:\n        return _wide_body(area)\n    if x < _SYMMETRIC_BODY_THRESHOLD:\n        return _symmetric_body(area)\n    return _grow_body(area)\n\n\ndef _marker_cell(body):\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = _bbox(body)\n    interior, exterior = set(), set()\n    for r, c in body:\n        for dr, dc in _NEIGHBORS4:\n            p = (r + dr, c + dc)\n            if p in body:\n                continue\n            if r0 <= p[0] <= r1 and c0 <= p[1] <= c1:\n                interior.add(p)\n            else:\n                exterior.add(p)\n    pool = list(interior if interior and random.random() < _MARKER_INTERIOR_PROB else (exterior | interior))\n    return random.choice(pool)\n\n\ndef _make_sprite(area, body_color, marker_color, bg):\n    body = _make_body(area)\n    marker = _marker_cell(body)\n    all_cells = set(body) | {marker}\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = _bbox(all_cells)\n    patch = np.full((r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1), int(bg), dtype=int)\n    for r, c in body:\n        patch[r - r0, c - c0] = int(body_color)\n    patch[marker[0] - r0, marker[1] - c0] = int(marker_color)\n    return {\"patch\": patch, \"offset\": (marker[0] - r0, marker[1] - c0)}\n\n\ndef _top_left(sprite, marker_r, marker_c):\n    off_r, off_c = sprite[\"offset\"]\n    return int(marker_r) - int(off_r), int(marker_c) - int(off_c)\n\n\ndef _can_place(canvas, sprite, marker_r, marker_c, bg):\n    patch = sprite[\"patch\"]\n    top, left = _top_left(sprite, marker_r, marker_c)\n    h, w = patch.shape\n    H, W = canvas.shape\n    if top < _INNER_BORDER_GAP or left < _INNER_BORDER_GAP:\n        return False\n    if top + h > H - _INNER_BORDER_GAP or left + w > W - _INNER_BORDER_GAP:\n        return False\n    mask = patch != int(bg)\n    view = canvas[top : top + h, left : left + w]\n    if bool((view[mask] != int(bg)).any()):\n        return False\n    return not _touches_foreground(canvas, mask, top, left, bg)\n\n\ndef _touches_foreground(canvas, mask, top, left, bg):\n    \"\"\"Return True if any patch cell has a non-bg 8-neighbor on canvas.\"\"\"\n    h, w = mask.shape\n    radius = _ISOLATION_RADIUS\n    occupied = canvas[top - radius : top + h + radius, left - radius : left + w + radius] != int(bg)\n    touch_zone = np.zeros((h + 2 * radius, w + 2 * radius), dtype=bool)\n    span = 2 * radius + 1\n    for dr in range(span):\n        for dc in range(span):\n            touch_zone[dr : dr + h, dc : dc + w] |= mask\n    return bool((occupied & touch_zone).any())\n\n\ndef _place(canvas, sprite, marker_r, marker_c, bg):\n    top, left = _top_left(sprite, marker_r, marker_c)\n    paste(canvas, sprite[\"patch\"], top, left, transparent=int(bg))\n\n\ndef _anchor_ok(canvas, r, c, bg):\n    H, W = canvas.shape\n    if not (r in (0, H - 1) or c in (0, W - 1)):\n        return False\n    if r in (0, H - 1) and c in (0, W - 1):\n        return False\n    return _isolated_bg_cell(canvas, r, c, bg)\n\n\ndef _isolated_bg_cell(canvas, r, c, bg):\n    \"\"\"Return True when a cell and its in-bounds 8-neighborhood are bg.\"\"\"\n    H, W = canvas.shape\n    radius = _ISOLATION_RADIUS\n    r0, r1 = max(0, r - radius), min(H, r + radius + 1)\n    c0, c1 = max(0, c - radius), min(W, c + radius + 1)\n    return not bool((canvas[r0:r1, c0:c1] != int(bg)).any())\n\n\ndef _anchor_candidates(canvas, bg):\n    H, W = canvas.shape\n    rows = list(range(_ANCHOR_EDGE_MARGIN, H - _ANCHOR_EDGE_MARGIN))\n    rows = rows or list(range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, H - _INNER_BORDER_GAP))\n    cols = list(range(_ANCHOR_EDGE_MARGIN, W - _ANCHOR_EDGE_MARGIN))\n    cols = cols or list(range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, W - _INNER_BORDER_GAP))\n    out = []\n    for c in cols:\n        out.append((\"h\", 0, c))\n        out.append((\"h\", H - 1, c))\n    for r in rows:\n        out.append((\"v\", r, 0))\n        out.append((\"v\", r, W - 1))\n    random.shuffle(out)\n    return [(axis, r, c) for axis, r, c in out if _anchor_ok(canvas, r, c, bg)]\n\n\ndef _put_anchor(canvas, r, c, color):\n    paste(canvas, np.array([[int(color)]], dtype=int), int(r), int(c))\n\n\ndef _aligned_positions(canvas, sprite, anchor, bg):\n    H, W = canvas.shape\n    if anchor[\"axis\"] == \"h\":\n        return [\n            (r, anchor[\"c\"])\n            for r in range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, H - _INNER_BORDER_GAP)\n            if _can_place(canvas, sprite, r, anchor[\"c\"], bg)\n        ]\n    return [\n        (anchor[\"r\"], c)\n        for c in range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, W - _INNER_BORDER_GAP)\n        if _can_place(canvas, sprite, anchor[\"r\"], c, bg)\n    ]\n\n\ndef _scatter_positions(canvas, sprite, anchor, marker, bg):\n    H, W = canvas.shape\n    mr, mc = marker\n    if anchor[\"axis\"] == \"h\":\n        return [\n            (mr, c)\n            for c in range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, W - _INNER_BORDER_GAP)\n            if c != mc and _can_place(canvas, sprite, mr, c, bg)\n        ]\n    return [\n        (r, mc)\n        for r in range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, H - _INNER_BORDER_GAP)\n        if r != mr and _can_place(canvas, sprite, r, mc, bg)\n    ]\n\n\ndef _body_color(bg, marker, used):\n    pool = [c for c in _COLORS if c not in {int(bg), int(marker)} and c not in used]\n    if not pool:\n        pool = [c for c in _COLORS if c not in {int(bg), int(marker)}]\n    return random.choice(pool)\n\n\ndef _bg_is_mode(grid, bg):\n    counts = Counter(map(int, grid.ravel()))\n    return counts[int(bg)] > max((n for c, n in counts.items() if c != int(bg)), default=0)\n\n\ndef _add_distractors(out, inp, anchors, bg):\n    vertical = [a for a in anchors if a[\"axis\"] == \"v\"]\n    if not vertical or random.random() >= _DISTRACTOR_PROB:\n        return\n    anchor = random.choice(vertical)\n    sprite = {\"patch\": np.array([[anchor[\"color\"]]], dtype=int), \"offset\": (0, 0)}\n    for _ in range(random.randint(*_DISTRACTOR_COUNT_RANGE)):\n        pairs = []\n        for c in range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, out.shape[1] - _INNER_BORDER_GAP):\n            if not _can_place(out, sprite, anchor[\"r\"], c, bg):\n                continue\n            for r in range(_INNER_BORDER_GAP, out.shape[0] - _INNER_BORDER_GAP):\n                if r != anchor[\"r\"] and _can_place(inp, sprite, r, c, bg):\n                    pairs.append((r, c))\n        if not pairs:\n            return\n        in_r, col = random.choice(pairs)\n        _place(out, sprite, anchor[\"r\"], col, bg)\n        _place(inp, sprite, in_r, col, bg)\n\n\ndef _gen_attempt():\n    bg, out, inp = _new_canvas_pair()\n    placed = _place_anchors(out, inp, bg)\n    if placed is None:\n        return None\n    anchor_colors, anchors = placed\n\n    marker_colors = _marker_color_sequence(anchor_colors)\n    sprites = _place_aligned_sprites(out, anchors, marker_colors, bg)\n    if sprites is None:\n        return None\n\n    if not _scatter_sprites(inp, sprites, bg):\n        return None\n\n    _add_distractors(out, inp, anchors, bg)\n    if not _generated_grid_is_valid(inp, out, bg):\n        return None\n    return inp\n\n\ndef _new_canvas_pair():\n    \"\"\"Choose grid size/background and return matching output/input canvases.\"\"\"\n    H = random.randint(*_GRID_HEIGHT_RANGE)\n    W = random.randint(*_GRID_WIDTH_RANGE)\n    bg = random.randint(*_BG_COLOR_RANGE)\n    out = np.full((H, W), int(bg), dtype=int)\n    inp = np.full((H, W), int(bg), dtype=int)\n    return bg, out, inp\n\n\ndef _place_anchors(out, inp, bg):\n    \"\"\"Place distinct isolated border anchors into both canvases.\"\"\"\n    anchor_colors = random.sample([c for c in _COLORS if c != bg], random.randint(*_ANCHOR_COUNT_RANGE))\n    anchors = []\n    for color in anchor_colors:\n        candidates = _anchor_candidates(out, bg)\n        if not candidates:\n            return None\n        axis, r, c = random.choice(candidates)\n        anchor = {\"color\": int(color), \"r\": int(r), \"c\": int(c), \"axis\": axis}\n        anchors.append(anchor)\n        _put_anchor(out, r, c, color)\n        _put_anchor(inp, r, c, color)\n    return anchor_colors, anchors\n\n\ndef _marker_color_sequence(anchor_colors):\n    \"\"\"Expand anchor colors to the sprite count, allowing repeated markers.\"\"\"\n    n_sprites = random.randint(*_SPRITE_COUNT_RANGE)\n    marker_colors = anchor_colors[:]\n    while len(marker_colors) < n_sprites:\n        marker_colors.append(random.choice(anchor_colors))\n    random.shuffle(marker_colors)\n    return marker_colors\n\n\ndef _place_aligned_sprites(out, anchors, marker_colors, bg):\n    \"\"\"Build sprites in their solved locations and return their align metadata.\"\"\"\n    by_color = {a[\"color\"]: a for a in anchors}\n    used_body = set()\n    sprites = []\n    for marker in marker_colors:\n        anchor = by_color[int(marker)]\n        body = _body_color(bg, marker, used_body)\n        used_body.add(body)\n        sprite = _make_sprite(random.randint(*_BODY_AREA_RANGE), body, marker, bg)\n        positions = _aligned_positions(out, sprite, anchor, bg)\n        if not positions:\n            return None\n        marker_pos = random.choice(positions)\n        _place(out, sprite, marker_pos[0], marker_pos[1], bg)\n        sprites.append((sprite, anchor, marker_pos))\n    return sprites\n\n\ndef _scatter_sprites(inp, sprites, bg):\n    \"\"\"Move solved sprites onto the input canvas along the inverse axis.\"\"\"\n    random.shuffle(sprites)\n    for sprite, anchor, marker_pos in sprites:\n        positions = _scatter_positions(inp, sprite, anchor, marker_pos, bg)\n        if not positions:\n            return False\n        in_pos = random.choice(positions)\n        _place(inp, sprite, in_pos[0], in_pos[1], bg)\n    return True\n\n\ndef _generated_grid_is_valid(inp, out, bg):\n    \"\"\"Apply generator invariants and the solver oracle check.\"\"\"\n    if not _bg_is_mode(inp, bg):\n        return False\n    return bool(np.array_equal(main(inp), out))\n\n\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    for _ in range(_GEN_RETRY_LIMIT):\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\n        if grid is not None:\n            return grid\n    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid 581f7754 input\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/1/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据彩色锚点确定镜像轴，将网格中的形状沿该轴翻转，翻转后的形状按锚点颜色重新上色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景色为 black。网格中散布着若干由单一颜色绘制的不规则连通形状（8-连通）。\n  - 网格边缘上放置着成对的小型彩色标记像素（每对由两个相同颜色的像素组成，分别位于网格的相对两侧边缘，如上-下或左-右），这些标记像素的颜色与网格内部形状的颜色不同。\n  - 每对边缘标记像素之间的连线定义了一条镜像轴（水平或垂直）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一层推理：识别边缘标记对。每对标记的两个像素位于网格的相对边缘、处于相同的行（左-右对）或相同的列（上-下对），连线形成一条隐含的镜像轴。\n  - 第二层推理：对于每个内部形状，判断它与哪条镜像轴\"关联\"。关联规则是：形状的边界框中心距离哪条镜像轴最近（在该轴的垂直方向上距离最近），该形状就属于那条轴。\n  - 第三层推理：将每个形状沿其关联的镜像轴做镜像翻转，翻转后的副本用该轴的标记颜色绘制。原始形状保留不变。若翻转后的副本与任何已有像素重叠，重叠处保留翻转副本的颜色。\n\n- `Key insight`：边缘标记对隐含地定义了镜像轴，而形状到轴的归属需要通过空间邻近性判断——解题者需要先发现\"成对标记 = 轴\"的编码方式，再发现\"就近归属\"的分配规则，最后才是执行翻转并重新着色。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内的种子颜色，沿墙壁缺口方向向外生长树状分支，分支长度由区域内种子像素数量决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景色为 black。网格中有若干由 grey 像素构成的不规则封闭围墙（连通的闭合边界），每个围墙恰好有一个缺口（缺少一个像素的位置）。\n  - 每个围墙内部有若干彩色种子像素（颜色各异，如 red、blue、green 等），散布在封闭区域内的不同位置。\n  - 围墙外部全是背景色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一层推理：对于每个封闭围墙，找到其唯一缺口的位置。缺口方向由缺口像素相对于围墙质心的方位决定（上、下、左、右四个基本方向之一）。\n  - 第二层推理：统计围墙内部每种颜色的种子像素数量。每种颜色的像素数量 N 决定了该颜色分支从缺口向外延伸的长度（N 个像素）。\n  - 第三层推理：从缺口位置开始，向缺口方向发射射线。多种颜色的射线并排排列：按颜色的种子像素在围墙内部从左到右（缺口朝上或朝下时）或从上到下（缺口朝左或朝右时）的位置顺序，依次排列在射线的垂直方向上。每条射线的长度等于对应颜色的种子像素数量。\n\n- `Key insight`：围墙缺口同时编码了生长方向，种子数量编码了生长长度，而种子在围墙内的空间排列顺序编码了射线的排列顺序——三层信息需要分别提取并组合。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落的彩色碎片按形状匹配嵌入模板框架的对应槽位中，然后根据槽位在框架中的相对位置（上半部或下半部）对碎片执行不同的颜色变换。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景色为 black。网格中有一个由 maroon 像素构成的大型矩形框架，框架内部被 maroon 像素分割成若干矩形槽位（类似货架格子）。每个槽位内部是背景色。\n  - 框架外部散布着若干彩色碎片（各碎片颜色不同，形状为不规则连通块）。每个碎片的边界框尺寸恰好与框架内某个槽位的尺寸一致。\n  - 框架的正上方有一行由两个颜色交替排列的像素条，形如\"A B A B...\"，A 和 B 各为一种非背景、非 maroon 的颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一层推理：将每个碎片按边界框尺寸匹配到框架中唯一对应的槽位（尺寸严格一致），将碎片放入该槽位中（保持碎片形状不变，左上角对齐槽位左上角）。\n  - 第二层推理：观察框架上方的交替色条。色条中的颜色 A 对应\"保持原色\"操作，颜色 B 对应\"将碎片颜色替换为 B\"操作。\n  - 第三层推理：每个槽位根据其所在的行位置（从上到下第几行）决定应用哪种操作：奇数行（第 1、3、5...行）的槽位中碎片保持原色，偶数行（第 2、4、6...行）的槽位中碎片被重新着色为颜色 B。输出仅包含填充完毕的框架区域。\n\n- `Key insight`：碎片嵌入是拼图匹配问题，但颜色变换规则需要从色条中解读\"奇偶行交替变色\"的隐含编码——色条的交替模式暗示了行方向的交替操作。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在网格中找到由不同颜色边框围成的嵌套矩形，按嵌套层级从外到内提取边框颜色序列，然后用该颜色序列重绘网格角落的指示条。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景色为 azure。网格中央有若干层嵌套的矩形边框，每层边框颜色不同（如最外层 red、次外层 green、再内层 yellow 等），边框宽度均为 1 像素。最内层矩形内部填充一种独特的颜色（如 orange）。\n  - 网格的四个角落各有一个小型 L 形指示条（由 grey 像素绘制，形如 2×2 区域缺少一个角的 3 像素 L 形）。四个 L 形分别朝向网格中心（即缺失角朝外）。\n  - 每个 L 形指示条旁边（沿其两条臂的延伸方向）有一小段由 grey 像素组成的直线尾巴，尾巴长度等于嵌套矩形的层数。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一层推理：识别嵌套矩形的层级结构。从最外层边框开始向内逐层读取每层边框的颜色，得到一个颜色序列（如 [red, green, yellow]）。\n  - 第二层推理：确定最内层填充色，将其追加到颜色序列末尾。\n  - 第三层推理：将每个角落 L 形指示条的 grey 尾巴像素按照该颜色序列依次重新着色——距离 L 形最近的尾巴像素着最外层颜色，依次向外着更内层的颜色。L 形本身保持 grey 不变。嵌套矩形区域在输出中保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需先发现中央嵌套结构编码了一个颜色序列，再发现角落尾巴的长度恰好等于嵌套层数并非巧合，而是需要用嵌套序列对尾巴像素逐一着色。嵌套层级的阅读方向（由外到内）与尾巴着色方向（由近到远）的对应关系是关键。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中的彩色路径段在交叉点处按照\"让路规则\"断开或连通，让路规则由路径段的优先级图例和交叉点旁的反转标记共同决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景色为 black。网格中有若干条由不同颜色绘制的直线路径段（水平或垂直，宽度为 1 像素）。部分路径段在网格中相互交叉（交叉点处两条路径共享同一个格子）。\n  - 网格的底部有一行\"优先级图例\"：从左到右排列着若干个 1×1 的彩色像素，颜色顺序对应路径的优先级（最左侧 = 最高优先级）。\n  - 在某些交叉点旁边（上下左右四邻域之一）放置了一个 magenta 像素作为\"反转标记\"。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一层推理：识别底部图例中的颜色优先级顺序。从左到右读取颜色，越靠左优先级越高。\n  - 第二层推理：对于每一个交叉点（两条不同颜色路径共享的格子），比较两条路径的优先级。如果该交叉点旁边没有 magenta 反转标记，则高优先级路径保留该格子的颜色，低优先级路径在该格子处断开（交叉点像素着高优先级路径的颜色，低优先级路径在交叉点两侧各缩回 1 个像素变为背景色）。\n  - 第三层推理：如果交叉点旁边存在 magenta 反转标记，则规则反转——低优先级路径保留该格子，高优先级路径在该处断开并缩回。输出中移除所有 magenta 标记和底部图例行。\n\n- `Key insight`：交叉点的处理需要两层判断——先从图例中推断颜色优先级，再根据 magenta 标记的有无决定是正常让路还是反转让路。反转标记作为\"例外触发器\"使得规则不能简单地用\"高优先级始终胜出\"来概括，迫使解题者发现标记的反转语义。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
